From: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: boot_mode: enter rockusb on BOOT_LOADER

Linux `reboot loader` writes BOOT_BL_DOWNLOAD (0x5242C301) to the rk3328
boot-mode register (GRF + 0x5c8 = 0xff1005c8). Mainline setup_boot_mode() only
handles BOOT_FASTBOOT and BOOT_UMS, so on a mainline u-boot the flag is
cleared and the unit simply boots again.

The DSGW-210 has no MaskROM button, so once this u-boot is on the eMMC a
software path back to USB flashing has to live in u-boot itself. Map
BOOT_LOADER to a preboot that serves rockusb on the OTG controller with the
eMMC (mmc 0) as the backing device, so `rkdeveloptool wl` works as it does
against the vendor loader.

Only compiled in with CONFIG_CMD_ROCKUSB. Requires BOARD_LATE_INIT (caller of
setup_boot_mode) and USE_PREBOOT.

Signed-off-by: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -105,6 +105,21 @@
 		debug("%s: enter UMS!\n", __func__);
 		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; ums mmc 0");
 		break;
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CMD_ROCKUSB)
+	case BOOT_LOADER:
+		/*
+		 * Linux `reboot loader` (syscon-reboot-mode, mode-loader =
+		 * BOOT_BL_DOWNLOAD) lands here. Serve rockusb on the OTG
+		 * controller, exposing the eMMC (mmc 0 = emmc@ff520000 per
+		 * the rk3328 u-boot aliases), so rkdeveloptool can re-flash
+		 * the unit over USB-C. After 300 s without host traffic
+		 * (DSGW-210 patch 0004) preboot returns and the normal
+		 * bootcmd runs.
+		 */
+		printf("boot mode: loader -> rockusb 0 mmc 0 300\n");
+		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; echo DSGW210-ROCKUSB: boot-mode loader, entering rockusb 0 mmc 0 300; rockusb 0 mmc 0 300");
+		break;
+#endif
 	}
 
 	return 0;
